Name: wgpu-hal
URL: https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu
Version: 30.0.0 (014d9e84813a2946febfa4888694c0b70565b2f5)
License: MIT OR Apache-2.0
License File: LICENSE.MIT, LICENSE.APACHE

This is the HAL from the exact wgpu revision used by the shell. Cargo.toml is
normalized to remove workspace inheritance; its internal naga/wgpu-types
dependencies still use that same Git revision. Workspace and fixture Cargo
patches replace only wgpu-hal, retaining the coherent upstream graph.

Local change: src/vulkan/descriptor.rs adds one unused sampler descriptor
when allocating a pool for an empty bind-group layout. Intel HD Graphics 530
with Windows driver 31.0.101.2111 otherwise crashes inside igvk64.dll during
vkCreateDescriptorPool. An independent Vulkan-only ctypes reproduction also
crashes with poolSizeCount=0 and succeeds with one sampler descriptor.
The extra descriptor does not alter any set layout or submitted GPU work.

Revalidate with the existing ignored direct pixel upload/readback test under
VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation, WGPU_VALIDATION=1, WGPU_DEBUG=1. See the Windows
progress log for commands and results. Local change: src/vulkan/instance.rs (`load_macos_vulkan`) locates the Vulkan
loader on macOS. ash opens `libvulkan.dylib` by leaf name, which dyld cannot
find in Homebrew's prefix or an app bundle, and macOS strips `DYLD_*` from
processes started through protected binaries. The helper tries
`FLUTTER_RUST_VULKAN_LIBRARY`, the default lookup, the executable directory,
`../Frameworks`, `/opt/homebrew/lib` and `/usr/local/lib`, in that order. It is
compiled only for `target_os = "macos"`.

No other source changes are intended.
